          <!-- ============================================================ Overview -->
          <section class="doc-section" id="overview">
            <h2>Overview</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              Xonus is a small, typed decision engine for Gemini. Give it a question and
              a fixed set of options; it returns the chosen option, the full probability
              distribution, and a <code>confident</code> flag you can safely branch on.
            </p>
            <p>
              Under the hood it reads token-level log probabilities, computes the
              log-odds margin between the top two options, and stops generating as soon
              as the answer is settled. Decisions that are not settled get one
              deliberation pass. A separate answer-mass gate checks that the model put
              its probability on valid options.
            </p>

            <CodeBlock code={snippets.hello} lang="ts" file="hello.ts" />

            <h3>Design principles</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Evidence over prose.</strong> The model's token distribution is
                the output, not a side effect to be discarded.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Deterministic by default.</strong> The fast pass uses temperature
                <code>0</code> and a single option letter.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Honest uncertainty.</strong> If logprobs are unavailable, Xonus
                returns <code>confidence: 0</code> instead of inventing a number.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>No hidden state.</strong> No global singleton, no agent loop, no
                storage. Every decision is a function call.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="callout">
              <span class="callout-icon">i</span>
              <div>
                <p>
                  Xonus is Gemini-native. It uses the
                  <code>@google/genai</code> SDK and the <code>responseLogprobs</code>
                  generation option. It is not a provider-agnostic router.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

