          <!-- ============================================================== Models -->
          <section class="doc-section" id="models">
            <h2>Models &amp; limits</h2>
            <p>
              The only hard requirement is that the model returns token log
              probabilities through <code>responseLogprobs</code>. The default,
              <code>gemini-2.5-flash</code>, supports it and balances latency, cost, and
              decision quality.
            </p>

            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Topic</th>
                    <th>Behavior</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Logprobs</td>
                    <td>
                      Requested with <code>topLogprobs</code> candidates (max 20). If the
                      model omits them, Xonus falls back to text and reports zero
                      confidence.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Thinking</td>
                    <td>
                      Disabled by default (<code>thinkingBudget: 0</code>) for predictable
                      cost and clean decision tokens. Override through
                      <code>generationConfig</code>.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Output limits</td>
                    <td>
                      Fast pass: 32 tokens max. Deliberation:
                      <code>maxOutputTokens</code> (default 512).
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Options</td>
                    <td>2–26, each non-empty and unique.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Streaming</td>
                    <td>Deliberation is always streamed so Xonus can abort early.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td>Cost</td>
                    <td>
                      One short request for confident decisions; two requests only when
                      escalation is needed. No sampling loop.
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
              <span class="callout-icon">i</span>
              <div>
                <p>
                  Xonus caps <code>logOdds</code> at <code>99</code> so the value survives
                  <code>JSON.stringify</code>. A capped value means the runner-up was
                  effectively zero; it is not a precision limit on the model.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

